  "content": "Here is the step-by-step deterministic arithmetic solution.\n\n**Given values:**\n*   $a = 137$\n*   $b = 29$\n*   $c = 11$\n\n**Expression to compute:**\n$$(a \\times b + c^3) - (a - b) \\times c$$\n\nWe will break this down into logical intermediate steps.\n\n### Step 1: Compute $a \\times b$\n$$137 \\times 29$$\n\nBreak down the multiplication:\n$$137 \\times 29 = 137 \\times (30 - 1)$$\n$$= (137 \\times 30) - (137 \\times 1)$$\n$$= 4110 - 137$$\n$$= 3973$$\n\nSo, $a \\times b = 3973$.\n\n### Step 2: Compute $c^3$\n$$11^3 = 11 \\times 11 \\times 11$$\n$$11 \\times 11 = 121$$\n$$121 \\times 11 = 1331$$\n\nSo, $c^3 = 1331$.\n\n### Step 3: Compute the first parenthesis $(a \\times b + c^3)$\nUsing the results from Step 1 and Step 2:\n$$3973 + 1331$$\n\nArithmetic:\n$$3973 + 1331 = 5304$$\n\nSo, the first term is $5304$.\n\n### Step 4: Compute $(a - b)$\n$$137 - 29$$\n\nArithmetic:\n$$137 - 29 = 108$$\n\nSo, $(a - b) = 108$.\n\n### Step 5: Compute the second term $((a - b) \\times c)$\nUsing the result from Step 4:\n$$108 \\times 11$$\n\nArithmetic:\n$$108 \\times 11 = 108 \\times (10 + 1)$$\n$$= (108 \\times 10) + (108 \\times 1)$$\n",
